  "$doc": "APPROVED client-write authorization boundary for protected tables. Enforced in CI by check:authorization-contract (src/scripts/checkAuthorizationContract.ts) against the live CI database. A migration that broadens anon/authenticated mutation privileges, exposes a server-derived column to client writes, or adds/changes an RLS policy on one of these tables will FAIL CI until this contract is updated in the same PR (an intentional, reviewed change). See migrations 2144-2154.",
  "$invariants": [
    "1. client table-level grants (anon/authenticated) must EQUAL the approved set (SELECT-only or narrower) — no restored INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE/TRUNCATE/REFERENCES/TRIGGER.",
    "2. client column INSERT/UPDATE grants must EQUAL the approved allowlist — a server-derived verification/provenance column must never become client-writable.",
    "3. the RLS policy set (name+cmd+roles+permissive) must EQUAL the approved set — a new permissive policy fails until added here."
